 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Sure. A complementary color is one that' opposite in hue to your primary color. For red, it' blue, for yellow, it's purple, and for green, it's orange. Mixing them together gives muted, dull colors. If you want something brighter, you add white from a white box, or black to darken. Definitely. A bit of complementary color mixed into your shades makes them pop against the red. Black paint is great, but it can make red look darker than you want.",
